<title>UK: Russia's Novorossiisk still shut, Tuapse reopens.</title>
<headline>Russia's Novorossiisk still shut, Tuapse reopens.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Black Sea port of Tuapse reopened on Tuesday but Russia's leading oil export terminal at Novorossiisk remained closed due to bad weather, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>Tuapse closed on Sunday because of bad weather. Novorossiisk, also on the Black Sea, was shut for most of the weekend due to high winds and swell, the source said.</p>
<p>The Novorossiisk terminal, which shut at 1800 (local) on Friday, reopened early on Sunday morning allowing two tankers to berth but then closed again at midday (local).</p>
<p>Nine tankers were at anchor outside Novorossiisk on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Odessa and the Baltic port of Ventspils were operating normally, the shipping source said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
